Thank you for the call.

As discussed, please confirm the following points:

1. Terminal Information / Flight Information for Connecting Flights

All connecting flight information belonging to the same trip group should be displayed in the check-in email. This should include:

Departure Airport
Arrival Airport
Flight Number
Departure Date & Time
Check-in Terminal

The terminal information should be identified using the getFlightInfo API for each connecting flight. If terminal information is not available from the API response, it is not required to display the terminal details in the connecting flight information section of the check-in email.

2. Check-in Details (Terminal, Airline, Channel)

Check-in Terminal

The terminal should be displayed when it is available from the getFlightInfo API response.
If terminal information is not available, it is not required to display the terminal in the check-in email.

Check-in Airline

The check-in airline should be displayed as "WY" for all passengers in the check-in email.

Check-in Channel

The check-in channel should be displayed as "Online" for all passengers in the check-in email.
3. Customer Seat Information

It is not required to display seat information in the check-in email for the time being.

4. Customer Baggage Allowance

The baggage allowance should be displayed as follows:

If the baggage allowance is 0, display 0.
Otherwise, display the baggage allowance along with the corresponding unit (e.g., 20 KG).
Email Address Identification

As discussed, the current flow is:

Check for the email address at the reservation level.
If not available, retrieve the email address from the passenger email attribute.

Going forward, if the email address is not available at the reservation level, it should be retrieved from the CTCE SSR instead of the passenger email attribute.

Example:

CTCE WY HK1/SATISH.DADAMODE//OMANAIR.COM

The email address should be derived from the CTCE value as:

SATISH.DADAMODE@OMANAIR.COM

